  "description": "A parametric BATHTUB on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nTHE SHELL IS FOUR RIM BARS AND A BASE, not a box with a hole. This language cannot subtract one polygon from another — booleans are a Merge / Boolean 2D node's job, never hand-rolled — so the rim is built as the four strips that surround the well and the well is its own piece. The plan then reads correctly at any shell thickness, and the well's own outline is available as a slot for anyone who needs the water line.\n\nTHE APRON IS A SEPARATE PIECE for the same reason it is on a real tub: it is the only part that changes between a tub against one wall, a tub in an alcove, and a sunken tub. Three options, one ternary, and \"None (sunken)\" simply lifts the apron's base to rim level so nothing is drawn below.\n\nWATER VOLUME is published at 70% of the well box — a filled tub is not a full one, and a figure that pretends otherwise is worse than none.",
